  },
  "question": "Specify a structured elicitation protocol (reference-class framing, independent priors, calibration questions, aggregation) for questions where no literature exists, and determine on 6 such questions whether elicited estimates add information over an honest NOT-FOUND. Distinct from the council bucket: this is a research-input mode, not a decision protocol.",
  "answer": "A four-step research-input protocol (reference-class framing, independent priors, calibration questions, Cooke/equal-weight aggregation) can be run with 4 sealed agent personas. On 6 unpublished worktree questions, public search is NOT-FOUND; elicitation added labeled priors but not measured evidence (3/6 intervals covered a later local census). On 2 literature controls, blind elicitation missed 1/2 known answers (Cooke 5/50/95 count). Adoption status=WEAK: the mode does not beat a search as a source class. Elicited values remain ELICITED-NOT-MEASURED. SUCCESS:RES-0182",
  "freshness_stamp": "2026-08-29T05:03:20Z",
  "protocol": {
    "reference_class_framing": {
      "description": "Each agent persona must name a reference class before stating quantiles. The class is recorded on the participant row and is the only allowed basis for the estimate.",
      "enforced_in": "participants.json reference_class field"
    },
    "independent_priors": {
      "description": "Personas are sealed: they do not read snapshots, each other's quantiles, or the local census until after aggregation.",
      "n_participants": 4,
      "cross_talk": false
    },
    "calibration_questions": {
      "description": "Four public seed quantities score each persona. Weight is calibration_rate times an inverse-width information score. Personas below 50% seed-interval hits are discounted to weight 0.",
